=== file: README.md ===
# Research brief with human approval

Run `Main` with a topic. The workflow researches it using public web search, drafts a sourced brief, asks a critic to identify material weaknesses, and has a reviser address the feedback while keeping the brief within 500 words.

A person reviews the revised brief. Only an explicit `approve` response returns it with the `APPROVED` label. Rejections trigger a revision using the requested changes, with at most two rejection-and-revision cycles. If both cycles are rejected, the latest brief is returned as `NOT APPROVED`. An empty topic prompts for one; an empty response halts the run. Research failures are retried at most twice and then halt without presenting an unsupported brief.

The project has no sending or writing effects. The only external access is the public `WebSearch` tool. The budget is capped at 20,000 tokens and 15 calls.

Run the workflow with `weave run main.loom --workflow Main --input research_subject="urban tree cover"` (use the input syntax supported by your installed `weave` version). Run the scripted workflow tests with `weave test main.loom`. Review the agent datasets with `weave eval main.loom --mock`.
=== end

